# Page-text recall receipt (search wiring W6c): a term that appears only in a
# page BODY recalls that page from the omnibar.
#
# Start scenarios/fixtures/trail_text_server.ps1 on port 43121 first; the run
# is otherwise loopback-only. FRESH profile.
#
# The fixture makes the claim unfakeable in both directions. HAGIOSCOPE is in
# the body of /notes/7 and in neither its path nor its title ("Field notes");
# PARBUCKLE is in the body of /notes/8 alone. A recall lane reading only titles
# and URLs answers nothing for either word, and one that pooled the bodies
# would answer the same page for both — so the two asserts together say the
# text reached the index AND stayed attached to its own address.
settle 30
key escape

# ---- 1. Visit both pages so the fetch path extracts and stores their text ---
open http://127.0.0.1:43121/notes/7
settle 60
open http://127.0.0.1:43121/notes/8
settle 60

# ---- 2. A body-only term recalls its own page --------------------------------
omnibar find
type hagioscope
settle 40
assert snap suggestions ~ recall http://127.0.0.1:43121/notes/7
capture 01_body_term_recalls_the_page
key escape
settle 10

# ---- 3. The other body-only term recalls the OTHER page ----------------------
omnibar find
type parbuckle
settle 40
assert snap suggestions ~ recall http://127.0.0.1:43121/notes/8
capture 02_the_other_body_term_recalls_the_other_page
key escape
settle 10
